          "text": "# SV-MATH-001 \u2014 ALLOW Gate Admissibility\n\n## Assumptions and claim boundary\n\nBecause no authoritative GCAT/BCAT specification was supplied, the following is a generated abstract formalization:\n\n1. GCAT and BCAT are state-indexed endomorphisms on engine entities.\n2. Geometric boundary preservation means that both transformations preserve boundary membership in both directions.\n3. Bounded divergence means that a single natural-number bound applies to the divergence of both transformations at the given state.\n4. Ontological consistency means that both transformations preserve each entity\u2019s ontology label.\n5. The canonical `ALLOW` evaluator returns `ALLOW` exactly when all three conditions hold.\n6. An external implementation inherits the theorem only if it conforms extensionally to that canonical evaluator.\n\nThus the three conditions are jointly complete **for the specified evaluator, and for conforming implementations**. No claim is made that an unspecified production GCAT/BCAT engine uses these semantics.\n\n## Lean 4 proof candidate\n\n```lean\nimport Mathlib\n\nnamespace StegVerse\nnamespace SVMATH001\n\nuniverse u v w\n\n/-\nGeneric preservation predicates. These also provide categorical-style\nidentity and composition laws for boundary and ontology preservation.\n-/\n\n/-- A predicate `P` is preserved and reflected by the endomorphism `f`. -/\ndef Preserves {\u03b1 : Type u} (P : \u03b1 \u2192 Prop) (f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1) : Prop :=\n  \u2200 x, P x \u2194 P (f x)\n\n/-- An ontology labelling is preserved by an endomorphism. -/\ndef OntologyPreserves\n    {\u03b1 : Type u} {\u03a9 : Type w}\n    (ontology : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03a9) (f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1) : Prop :=\n  \u2200 x, ontology (f x) = ontology x\n\n/-- Identity preserves every predicate. -/\ntheorem Preserves.id\n    {\u03b1 : Type u} (P : \u03b1 \u2192 Prop) :\n    Preserves P id := by\n  intro x\n  rfl\n\n/--\nCategorical composition law for predicate-preserving endomorphisms.\n\nIf `f` and `g` preserve and reflect `P`, then `g \u2218 f` also preserves\nand reflects `P`.\n-/\ntheorem Preserves.comp\n    {\u03b1 : Type u} {P : \u03b1 \u2192 Prop} {f g : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1}\n    (hf : Preserves P f)\n    (hg : Preserves P g) :\n    Preserves P (g \u2218 f) := by\n  intro x\n  exact (hf x).trans (hg (f x))\n\n/-- Identity preserves every ontology labelling. -/\ntheorem OntologyPreserves.id\n    {\u03b1 : Type u} {\u03a9 : Type w}\n    (ontology : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03a9) :\n    OntologyPreserves ontology id := by\n  intro x\n  rfl\n\n/--\nCategorical composition law for ontology-preserving endomorphisms.\n-/\ntheorem OntologyPreserves.comp\n    {\u03b1 : Type u} {\u03a9 : Type w}\n    {ontology : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03a9} {f g : \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b1}\n    (hf : OntologyPreserves ontology f)\n    (hg : OntologyPreserves ontology g) :\n    OntologyPreserves ontology (g \u2218 f) := by\n  intro x\n  calc\n    ontology ((g \u2218 f) x) = ontology (g (f x)) := rfl\n    _ = ontology (f x) := hg (f x)\n    _ = ontology x := hf x\n\n/--\nAbstract GCAT/BCAT engine signature.\n\nNo metric axioms are required for SV-MATH-001. The `distance` field is\nthe selected natural-number-valued divergence measure.\n-/\nstructure Engine where\n  Entity   : Type u\n  State    : Type v\n  Ontology : Type w\n\n  gcat : State \u2192 Entity \u2192 Entity\n  bcat : State \u2192 Entity \u2192 Entity\n\n  boundary : State \u2192 Entity \u2192 Prop\n  distance : Entity \u2192 Entity \u2192 Nat\n  ontology : Entity \u2192 Ontology\n\n/--\nGeometric boundary preservation at state `s`.\n\nBoth GCAT and BCAT preserve and reflect membership in the geometric\nboundary selected by `s`.\n-/\ndef GeometricBoundaryPreservation\n    (e : Engine) (s : e.State) : Prop :=\n  Preserves (e.boundary s) (e.gcat s) \u2227\n  Preserves (e.boundary s) (e.bcat s)\n\n/--\nBounded divergence at state `s`.\n\nOne finite natural-number bound must bound the GCAT and BCAT divergence\nof every entity.\n-/\ndef BoundedDivergence\n    (e : Engine) (s : e.State) : Prop :=\n  \u2203 K : Nat,\n    (\u2200 x : e.Entity, e.distance x (e.gcat s x) \u2264 K) \u2227\n    (\u2200 x : e.Entity, e.distance x (e.bcat s x) \u2264 K)\n\n/--\nOntological consistency at state `s`.\n\nGCAT and BCAT must preserve the ontology label of every entity.\n-/\ndef OntologicalConsistency\n    (e : Engine) (s : e.State) : Prop :=\n  OntologyPreserves e.ontology (e.gcat s) \u2227\n  OntologyPreserves e.ontology (e.bcat s)\n\n/-- The conjunction of all three ALLOW conditions. -/\ndef JointConditions\n    (e : Engine) (s : e.State) : Prop :=\n  GeometricBoundaryPreservation e s \u2227\n  BoundedDivergence e s \u2227\n  OntologicalConsistency e s\n\n/-- Observable gate result. -/\ninductive GateResult where\n  | ALLOW\n  | DENY\nderiving DecidableEq, Repr\n\n/--\nCanonical GCAT/BCAT gate evaluator.\n\nClassical decidability is used because the conditions quantify over\npossibly infinite entity types.\n-/\nnoncomputable def evaluate\n    (e : Engine) (s : e.State) : GateResult :=\n  if JointConditions e s then\n    GateResult.ALLOW\n  else\n    GateResult.DENY\n\n/-- A state is gate-admissible when the canonical evaluator returns ALLOW. -/\ndef Admissible\n    (e : Engine) (s : e.State) : Prop :=\n  evaluate e s = GateResult.ALLOW\n\n/--\nMain necessary-and-sufficient theorem.\n\nThe ALLOW gate is admissible exactly when geometric boundary\npreservation, bounded divergence, and ontological consistency all hold.\n-/\ntheorem admissible_iff_joint_conditions\n    (e : Engine) (s : e.State) :\n    Admissible e s \u2194 JointConditions e s := by\n  classical\n  by_cases h : JointConditions e s\n  \u00b7 simp [Admissible, evaluate, h]\n  \u00b7 simp [Admissible, evaluate, h]\n\n/-- Geometric boundary preservation is necessary for ALLOW. -/\ntheorem admissible_implies_geometric\n    (e : Engine) (s : e.State)\n    (h : Admissible e s) :\n    GeometricBoundaryPreservation e s := by\n  have hj : JointConditions e s :=\n    (admissible_iff_joint_conditions e s).mp h\n  exact hj.1\n\n/-- Bounded divergence is necessary for ALLOW. -/\ntheorem admissible_implies_bounded\n    (e : Engine) (s : e.State)\n    (h : Admissible e s) :\n    BoundedDivergence e s := by\n  have hj : JointConditions e s :=\n    (admissible_iff_joint_conditions e s).mp h\n  exact hj.2.1\n\n/-- Ontological consistency is necessary for ALLOW. -/\ntheorem admissible"
